# Paths that are never gated components (D-32, pipeline/prompts/setup.md,
# docs/QA-FLOW.md). Same convention as Nocka's root nocka.exclude.
#
# Anchored to the target root (leading "/") — a top-level directory only; an
# unanchored pattern would also match a same-named directory nested anywhere
# else in the tree, which the pre-flat-file matcher never did.
#
# /temp/ is the Nocka pipeline's own scratch space: SDLC writes temp/qa/ (the QA
# run index plus pointers to the raw reports) fresh on every QA pass. It is
# control-plane output, not the task's code, and is never a gated component.
# Mirrors the `temp/` entry in .gitignore — keep the two in step.
#
# Added 2026-10-18 (nocka_task 5bc71d4e QA pass): the QA run index itself warned
# that `git check-ignore` could not confirm temp/ was excluded, so writing it
# surfaced as an untracked change under the settle dirty-tree check.
/temp/
